# Release notes

`.release-notes.md` is the GitHub release body. Write only key changes for this version. 

Use this shape:

```
### What's in <version>

<short summary>

- **<feature>**  - <description>
- **<feature>**  - <description>

[Website](https://arduloops.web.app/) · [GitHub](https://github.com/ArduLoops) · [Telegram](https://t.me/ArduLoops) · [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/@ArduLoops) · [♥ Support](https://arduloops.web.app/support)

Questions, feedback, and suggestions: [open an issue](https://github.com/ArduLoops/ArduLoops/issues/new).
```

The links line is the same in every release. GitHub links the organisation, not one repository. Support is the last link and the only mention of it: no request in the summary or the bullets (owner, 2026-11-24).

The summary is one or two short sentences. Each bullet is one feature. The description uses ASD-STE100: short sentences, one idea each, simple verbs, no marketing, no extra detail.

# Telegram post

`release/telegram/post.md` and `release/telegram/post.jpg` are the post for the Telegram group. The release job sends them after the installers are on the release (`.github/workflows/telegram.yml`). Update both in the same commit as `.release-notes.md`.

- `post.md`: the heading `### Що нового в <version>` (the post stops if the version is not the tag), one short sentence, and 3–6 points `- **<назва>** — <опис>` from the release notes. Plain Ukrainian for pilots.
- Keep only what a pilot gains: what they can now do or see. Leave out internal fixes, signing, build, bridge, protocol and parser details, and technical terms that the UI does not show (owner, 2026-11-24). Such changes stay in `.release-notes.md`. Use the Ukrainian UI labels from `src/i18n/uk.ts`; «борт», not «плата». The download link is added when it is sent.
- `post.jpg`: made in the video pipeline like a YouTube thumbnail (`node telegram.mjs --ui <capture>` in `demo/`), with real app captures.
